course: dictionary
lesson: 12229
title: Conserved: kept safe and kept the same
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Conserved is a word with three jobs, and the context tells you which one. Read the words around it first. «The rangers said the forest must be conserved for future visitors.» Forest and future visitors show that conserved means protected and kept safe, not thrown away or spoiled.
explain: In science, conserved means the total stays the same. «In the experiment, the total mass was conserved.» Nothing was lost and nothing was made, so the weight at the end was the same as at the start. A scientist would say the mass was conserved.
explain: In biology, conserved means kept almost the same for a very long time. «The gene is conserved, so it looks almost the same in many different animals.» The clue is the long time: the gene has stayed much the same across many kinds of living things.
fact: Conserved is the past form of the verb conserve.
fact: «Conserved» can mean protected and kept safe from damage or waste.
fact: In science, «energy is conserved» means the total amount stays the same, not made or destroyed.
fact: In biology, «conserved» can mean kept almost the same over a very long time.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simple meaning, such as «kept safe», and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The rangers said the forest must be conserved for future visitors.» What does conserved mean here? | *Protected and kept safe | Painted bright green | Chopped down and sold | Made into a road
exercise: «In the experiment, the total mass was conserved.» What does conserved mean in this science sentence? | Doubled in size | Became heavier every second | Disappeared into the air | *Stayed the same in total, not made or destroyed
exercise: «We saved the water and conserved it for the dry months.» Find and copy the word that means saved from waste. | *conserved | water | summer | months
test: «The gene is conserved in many animals, so it looks almost the same over a very long time.» What does conserved mean in biology? | Quickly changed | *Kept almost the same over a very long time | Lost forever | Made from scratch
test: Ella says «energy is conserved» means energy gets used up. Is she right? | *No, it means the total stays the same, not made or destroyed | Yes, energy is used up and gone | No, energy is never mentioned in science | Yes, energy is made new each day
exam: Which word is the past form of the verb conserve? | conservative | conservation | conservatory | *conserved
